{
 "id": "tenochtitlan",
 "note": "Claude draft (unchecked). Water areas give Lake Texcoco and the western Lake of Mexico around the island city c. 1519 (with the island cut out), the shallows later reclaimed by chinampas, and successively smaller colonial and 19th-century lake extents, each alive only for its period; today's terrain is dry lake bed. Island outlines follow the usual reconstructions (Mundy 2015) and are approximate; causeway routes follow surviving streets (Calzada de Guadalupe, México-Tacuba, San Antonio Abad). Peñón de los Baños and other small lake islands are not cut out of the lake.",
